1
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:04,850
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,390 --> 00:00:10,450
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,620
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:17,400
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:21,500
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:27,710
Guts...

7
00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:29,540
...are you thinking of...

8
00:00:37,050 --> 00:00:40,730
Are you going to leave
the Band of the Hawk?

9
00:01:01,410 --> 00:01:03,500
Feel no shame about shape

10
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:05,410
Weather changes their phrase

11
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:09,170
Even mother will show you another way

12
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:11,550
So put your glasses on

13
00:01:11,630 --> 00:01:13,630
Nothing will be wrong

14
00:01:13,710 --> 00:01:15,840
There's no blame. There's no fame

15
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:17,680
It's up to you

16
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:21,310
The first words should be found

17
00:01:21,930 --> 00:01:24,930
Whatever holds you back

18
00:01:25,810 --> 00:01:26,310
I...

19
00:01:26,690 --> 00:01:27,440
...can...

20
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:29,610
I can get it off

21
00:01:29,610 --> 00:01:30,610
Tell me what...

22
00:01:30,610 --> 00:01:31,610
Tell me what...

23
00:01:31,610 --> 00:01:33,440
Tell me what you want

24
00:01:33,570 --> 00:01:34,530
I don't know why...

25
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:35,530
Don't know why...

26
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:37,530
Don't know why you're afraid

27
00:01:37,700 --> 00:01:38,700
Tell me what...

28
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:39,660
Tell me what...

29
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:41,330
Tell me what you'd say

30
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:42,660
I don't know why...

31
00:01:42,790 --> 00:01:43,740
Don't know why...

32
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:44,540
Too late...

33
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:46,160
It's too late

34
00:01:51,090 --> 00:01:55,090
The Decisive Battle

35
00:02:23,990 --> 00:02:24,910
Message!

36
00:02:24,910 --> 00:02:25,580
Message!

37
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,080
I have a report!

38
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,830
Our army has endured immense damage!

39
00:02:28,830 --> 00:02:31,170
Only this headquarters remains intact!

40
00:02:31,170 --> 00:02:33,380
How could this have happened?

41
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:37,840
We White Tiger Knights have one of
the strongest armies in all Midland...

42
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:39,930
...and we have been beaten so easily!

43
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:43,600
That castle of Doldrey is quite impregnable!

44
00:02:43,890 --> 00:02:45,010
I have a report!

45
00:02:45,310 --> 00:02:46,640
Now what?

46
00:02:47,930 --> 00:02:50,690
A thousand cavalrymen from
the enemy fort's main gate!

47
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:53,440
They are charging our headquarters!

48
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:55,980
What?

49
00:02:55,980 --> 00:02:57,990
The strongest of all Tudor's armies...

50
00:02:57,990 --> 00:02:59,820
The Purple Rhino Knights?

51
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:33,230
This hundred-year war...

52
00:03:33,230 --> 00:03:37,020
...was triggered by the Tudor Empire's
invasion on Midland's territory.

53
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:40,070
The castle of Doldrey once belonged...

54
00:03:40,070 --> 00:03:42,660
...to our kingdom as
an integral part of our defenses.

55
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:45,160
Ironically, this fort has
become a staging point...

56
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:48,950
...for attacks by the Tudor army
ever since they captured it.

57
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:53,210
However, civil war may break forth
at any moment in the Tudor Empire...

58
00:03:53,210 --> 00:03:55,170
...in regards to the matter
of imperial succession.

59
00:03:55,460 --> 00:03:58,380
Most likely, the empire cannot...

60
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:03,050
...afford to spare all of its
great military forces for this war.

61
00:04:03,050 --> 00:04:05,720
Indeed, this is
a rare opportunity for us!

62
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:08,220
We can't miss this opportunity
to achieve the conquest of Doldrey!

63
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:10,640
No, to recapture our fief!

64
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:12,810
Very well, what shall we do about it?

65
00:04:12,810 --> 00:04:15,400
The principal garrison stationed
there is the Purple Rhino Knights.

66
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:18,070
They're led by fierce General Boscone
and are the strongest knights...

67
00:04:18,070 --> 00:04:19,730
...in the entire empire!

68
00:04:19,730 --> 00:04:21,780
Even our most powerful asset...

69
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:24,240
...the White Tiger Knights, suffered
great losses when engaging them.

70
00:04:25,610 --> 00:04:27,370
An all-out attack...

71
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:28,990
That might be our only option.

72
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:30,740
That is very risky!

73
00:04:31,410 --> 00:04:33,080
You must consider the overall campaign...

74
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:35,670
...as we've already lost forty percent
of our total fighting strength.

75
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,250
There is no guarantee...

76
00:04:37,250 --> 00:04:39,750
...that we will conquer Doldrey,
even if we deploy all of our assets.

77
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:41,300
If the battle is prolonged...

78
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:45,380
We will likely be caught between their
main army and the occupation forces!

79
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:47,970
If we are rash, we'll risk the
annihilation of our entire armed forces.

80
00:04:47,970 --> 00:04:51,720
I believe the war is overall in our favor,
and eventually we shall be victorious.

81
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:54,180
Therefore, such a dangerous
gamble is not worth the risk.

82
00:04:54,180 --> 00:04:59,060
But our final objective in this war
is to take control of Doldrey!

83
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:02,360
To recapture our fief,
occupying Doldrey is essential!

84
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:05,150
However, which unit will be
considered for the role of the vanguard?

85
00:05:05,150 --> 00:05:07,870
Remember, we lost
the White Tiger Knights.

86
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:08,990
Well...

87
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,500
What would you say, Sir Griffith?

88
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:19,290
Even your invincible Band of the Hawk
wouldn't be able to handle this, right?

89
00:05:20,290 --> 00:05:22,340
We could, if given the order.

90
00:05:22,340 --> 00:05:25,130
I understand. It can't be helped...

91
00:05:25,130 --> 00:05:25,920
Hey...

92
00:05:31,010 --> 00:05:33,560
If Your Majesty gives me the order...

93
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:34,640
Nonsense!

94
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:36,100
Do you think you can really do it?

95
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,730
Your Lordship understands
nothing about the difficulties!

96
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:41,150
He has gotten a rather swelled head...

97
00:05:41,150 --> 00:05:44,490
...on account of his
lucky victories in the past.

98
00:05:44,490 --> 00:05:45,280
I agree.

99
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:48,320
During the past one hundred years,
that castle has never been damaged...

100
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:51,580
...despite all of our many
desperate attempts to capture it.

101
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:53,200
However, you still say you can conquer it?

102
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,580
My Lord Griffith...

103
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:59,330
Can you truly do this?

104
00:06:01,590 --> 00:06:03,300
He is being reckless, Your Majesty!

105
00:06:03,710 --> 00:06:07,130
The Doldrey conquest requires us
to employ an enormous armed force!

106
00:06:07,130 --> 00:06:10,930
If we fail at this time, it will cause
great permanent damage to us...

107
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:14,680
I do not need to engage
them with a large army.

108
00:06:15,430 --> 00:06:18,770
The Band of the Hawk alone
will cope with this matter.

109
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:20,020
What?

110
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:20,850
That's impossible!

111
00:06:20,850 --> 00:06:21,980
Who do you think you are?

112
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,900
Don't be ridiculous!

113
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:26,900
A mere force of five thousand men...

114
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:30,530
...against the enemy's occupation
force of thirty thousand strong?

115
00:06:32,450 --> 00:06:34,240
Don't get cocky, boy!

116
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:39,120
And don't think your cunning
little schemes will succeed forever!

117
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,040
General...

118
00:06:41,420 --> 00:06:44,130
There's no need
to get up in arms over this.

119
00:06:44,130 --> 00:06:45,000
What?

120
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:48,470
Sooner or later, we will
have to venture into total war.

121
00:06:48,470 --> 00:06:51,140
We are left with
no other options in this matter.

122
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:56,140
But having a single troop
first carry out such a clever ploy...

123
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:58,600
...should not affect
the overall leadership of this army.

124
00:06:59,020 --> 00:07:03,110
And considering the Band of
the Hawk's past achievements...

125
00:07:03,110 --> 00:07:05,900
...it's unfair to say that
they will have no chance at all.

126
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:07,730
Do not underestimate Doldrey!

127
00:07:09,450 --> 00:07:10,400
Damn...

128
00:07:11,490 --> 00:07:13,950
Your Majesty, please give us your final word.

129
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:28,710
I command that the Band of the Hawk
be committed to Doldrey's conquest.

130
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,850
His Majesty has certainly aged.

131
00:07:34,850 --> 00:07:37,930
How could he rely upon
a newcomer, a boy like him?

132
00:07:38,350 --> 00:07:41,310
The army of Midland has lost all dignity.

133
00:07:46,270 --> 00:07:47,520
Well...

134
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:50,940
I can imagine how he feels,
but there's nothing that can be done...

135
00:07:51,450 --> 00:07:53,780
You have quite a high opinion
of that man, don't you?

136
00:07:54,530 --> 00:07:59,660
I wonder if the White Hawk will rise
to the occasion, as you expect he will.

137
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:04,120
Well, either way, I told them the truth.

138
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,920
Even if he loses the battle...

139
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:09,510
No other man in Midland...

140
00:08:09,510 --> 00:08:11,840
...is even capable of conquering Doldrey.

141
00:08:12,630 --> 00:08:13,510
Certainly.

142
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:31,990
It may be strange for a man to say this...

143
00:08:32,650 --> 00:08:35,320
...but he looks as if
he just stepped out of a painting.

144
00:08:35,660 --> 00:08:37,490
A commander beyond all others...

145
00:08:38,830 --> 00:08:44,080
Perhaps, we are fighting
alongside the kind of hero...

146
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:46,960
...who only emerges once in a century.

147
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:49,880
Doldrey, huh?

148
00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:52,300
Whatever, it makes no difference to me.

149
00:08:53,010 --> 00:08:56,470
Anyone can win a war
or dice game if it's meant to be!

150
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,600
There!

151
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,310
There you go!

152
00:09:02,770 --> 00:09:03,810
Get outta here!

153
00:09:03,810 --> 00:09:05,560
Winning ten times in a row?

154
00:09:05,560 --> 00:09:08,150
The commander won everything again.

155
00:09:09,270 --> 00:09:11,530
You really have the devil's own luck, boss!

156
00:09:11,530 --> 00:09:12,320
All right!

157
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:14,360
I won't give up until I get my money back!

158
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,110
What's wrong?

159
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:19,830
Is there something bothering you?

160
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:21,330
N-No...

161
00:09:21,910 --> 00:09:23,540
Don't worry.

162
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:27,290
We've been through
this kind of thing before.

163
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:31,380
If a self-respecting man
like him offered to fight...

164
00:09:31,380 --> 00:09:33,130
The odds must be in his favor.

165
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:38,970
I hope he doesn't lose his composure...

166
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:44,680
Do you remember what
I told you some time ago?

167
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:50,440
When we became involved in
a territorial dispute in a certain region...

168
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:52,900
Griffith...

169
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,150
I mean...

170
00:09:54,570 --> 00:09:56,740
That nobleman you mentioned...

171
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:59,490
Shit, the commander won again?

172
00:09:59,490 --> 00:10:01,830
Give me a break!

173
00:10:01,830 --> 00:10:05,580
That nobleman was promoted
to governor in a certain empire...

174
00:10:06,330 --> 00:10:09,790
His bribe money spoke the loudest
when the position was awarded.

175
00:10:11,790 --> 00:10:13,340
Hey, don't tell me he...

176
00:10:14,630 --> 00:10:19,380
The governor of the empire of
Tudor's northlands, Governor Gennon.

177
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:23,060
That's the title he currently holds.

178
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:35,030
Sir Adon, we are glad to see you safe.

179
00:10:35,570 --> 00:10:38,570
I, known far and wide as the
invulnerable and resourceful Adon...

180
00:10:38,570 --> 00:10:40,990
...would never die so easily!

181
00:10:41,490 --> 00:10:43,700
Anyway, that boy...

182
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:48,370
If we meet on the battlefield again,
I certainly won't let him get away!

183
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:51,000
For shame, Adon!

184
00:10:57,510 --> 00:10:59,840
Your Grace, General Boscone!

185
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:02,010
To settle a personal grudge...

186
00:11:02,010 --> 00:11:07,140
You deployed all those mercenaries,
and all you achieved was total defeat!

187
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:10,850
Even worse than that,
your brother Samson is dead!

188
00:11:10,850 --> 00:11:13,900
You've got a lot of nerve
coming back here alone...

189
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:15,690
...after such a disgrace!

190
00:11:15,690 --> 00:11:17,030
No, uh...

191
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:20,150
I-It is not true, Your Grace...

192
00:11:20,150 --> 00:11:21,110
Truthfully...

193
00:11:22,410 --> 00:11:24,280
This is outrageous!

194
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:42,630
From now on, I divest you of any
authority to command in this war.

195
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:46,640
You should appreciate the fact I'm
not throwing you in the dungeons!

196
00:11:52,390 --> 00:11:56,900
Your foe was reportedly only one
soldier, the same man in the rumors...

197
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:58,860
That cannot be...

198
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:07,120
You were strict as usual.

199
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:08,910
I could even hear you
shouting from up here.

200
00:12:09,910 --> 00:12:12,540
Please excuse my harsh manner.
It must be unpleasant to your ear.

201
00:12:12,910 --> 00:12:14,370
All right then.

202
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:19,250
By the way, according to my spies...

203
00:12:19,250 --> 00:12:24,180
...the second wave for the conquest
of Doldrey has been chosen.

204
00:12:27,390 --> 00:12:29,680
You know them well by now...

205
00:12:30,270 --> 00:12:31,390
...the Band of the Hawk.

206
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:35,350
You look happy.

207
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:38,150
No, I do not mean to...

208
00:12:38,150 --> 00:12:40,980
But they seem to be much
more difficult to deal with...

209
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:44,110
...than the other opponents, who
rely only on numbers and reputation.

210
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:52,330
Anyhow, I need to tell you something
before you set off for battle.

211
00:12:53,870 --> 00:12:58,130
The Band of the Hawk's leader,
Griffith the White Hawk...

212
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:01,510
You must not kill him.

213
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:06,010
Keep him alive and bring him to me.

214
00:13:06,380 --> 00:13:07,260
But...

215
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:10,680
Keep in mind this is your governor's order.

216
00:13:38,790 --> 00:13:40,790
How are your wounds? Still hurts?

217
00:13:41,130 --> 00:13:43,170
I'm fine now.

218
00:13:43,590 --> 00:13:45,720
Thanks to the medicine you gave me.

219
00:13:46,130 --> 00:13:50,140
Even so, the more I see
that fortress, the less confident I feel.

220
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:54,930
The castle walls are built twice as
high and twice as thick than any other.

221
00:13:54,930 --> 00:13:56,890
The far side is protected by a sheer cliff...

222
00:13:56,890 --> 00:14:00,110
And the Purple Rhinos
are stationed there as well.

223
00:14:00,110 --> 00:14:03,230
No big deal. It's just like
any other castle, only bigger.

224
00:14:03,230 --> 00:14:05,610
We'll just do what we always do.

225
00:14:05,610 --> 00:14:07,200
I hope so, anyway.

226
00:14:12,740 --> 00:14:15,040
Either way, I'm surprised.

227
00:14:15,750 --> 00:14:17,500
He burned all the boats.

228
00:14:21,170 --> 00:14:23,920
What on earth is the White Hawk thinking?

229
00:14:24,550 --> 00:14:28,300
I wonder if his tactic is to position
himself with his back to the river?

230
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:30,090
It doesn't matter.

231
00:14:30,090 --> 00:14:32,680
With their numbers, they can only
stave off the inevitable for a moment.

232
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:36,140
All we have to do
is attack them head-on.

233
00:14:36,930 --> 00:14:38,060
However...

234
00:14:38,770 --> 00:14:43,190
Does the governor happen
to have some relation to him?

235
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:48,450
Well, it's a waste of time for me
to worry about such absurdities!

236
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:53,950
My duty is only to tear
my opponents apart until the end!

237
00:14:59,370 --> 00:15:00,920
The White Hawk...

238
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:05,210
I have never imagined that
I would see him alive again.

239
00:15:06,050 --> 00:15:07,760
I'll definitely have him.

240
00:15:09,050 --> 00:15:11,300
Look at all of this dust!

241
00:15:12,260 --> 00:15:14,010
It's part of my plan.

242
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:17,720
Are you all right?

243
00:15:24,230 --> 00:15:25,230
Good.

244
00:15:25,230 --> 00:15:26,610
It's about time to move.

245
00:15:33,530 --> 00:15:36,870
I hope he doesn't lose his composure...

246
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:39,080
That will never happen.

247
00:15:39,450 --> 00:15:42,250
He's the last man to lose his calm...

248
00:15:49,010 --> 00:15:50,340
This is the final time...

249
00:15:53,590 --> 00:15:55,850
...I wield my sword under this flag...

250
00:15:56,470 --> 00:15:58,100
First formation, advance!

251
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:06,770
But I'm not going to leave
any loose ends behind me...

252
00:16:07,610 --> 00:16:11,030
I'm going to take full responsibility
as the leader of the Raiders!

253
00:16:12,490 --> 00:16:13,530
Draw your swords!

254
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:18,620
First formation, charge!

255
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:22,870
The first formation contains...

256
00:16:22,870 --> 00:16:26,330
...two thousand men directly under
Griffith and his top companies' control!

257
00:16:26,330 --> 00:16:27,790
What nonsense...

258
00:16:27,790 --> 00:16:31,300
Dividing his army into two formations
when he only has five thousand men?

259
00:16:32,010 --> 00:16:35,340
I don't know what kind of
cunning plan he's trying to hatch...

260
00:16:36,010 --> 00:16:38,140
Very well, I'll accept your challenge!

261
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:39,720
All units, charge!

262
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:41,890
Grind the enemy's first formation into dust!

263
00:16:49,900 --> 00:16:52,900
Are these their Raiders
we've heard so many reports about?

264
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:53,820
Interesting!

265
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:11,800
One of the enemy's companies
is bursting through our front line!

266
00:17:12,210 --> 00:17:15,680
They're aiming to get at our army's
leaders by breaking through head-on...

267
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:17,680
Is this the White Hawk's scheme?

268
00:17:29,110 --> 00:17:31,070
Follow the commander!

269
00:17:35,450 --> 00:17:36,490
This can't be!

270
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:39,870
Nothing has ever obstructed
the Purple Rhino's assault before...

271
00:17:39,870 --> 00:17:42,330
We can't move any further.
In fact, we might even be repelled!

272
00:17:42,330 --> 00:17:43,200
General!

273
00:17:43,790 --> 00:17:44,910
That's him.

274
00:17:46,250 --> 00:17:51,040
Reportedly, he wiped out one hundred
mercenaries all by himself...

275
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:53,250
It seems that report was not altogether false.

276
00:17:53,250 --> 00:17:56,010
Well, the White Hawk possesses good personnel.

277
00:17:56,510 --> 00:17:57,880
Remain steadfast!

278
00:17:57,880 --> 00:18:00,390
They're just trying to disrupt our training!

279
00:18:00,390 --> 00:18:03,430
Fall back into formation, then counterattack!

280
00:18:05,310 --> 00:18:09,440
They put up a good fight
against the Purple Rhino Knights...

281
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:13,230
But they will soon realize their limits.

282
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:19,360
Damn you, Boscone! At this rate,
you could end up killing Griffith!

283
00:18:21,740 --> 00:18:23,120
Someone, attend to me!

284
00:18:23,410 --> 00:18:24,410
Yes, sir!

285
00:18:25,290 --> 00:18:28,460
Have my personal guard
prepare to take the field.

286
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:32,130
I will command directly from the battlefield!

287
00:18:33,170 --> 00:18:35,630
However, what about defending the castle?

288
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:37,050
Pay no mind!

289
00:18:37,630 --> 00:18:40,510
As things stand, the Band of the Hawk cannot...

290
00:18:40,510 --> 00:18:42,890
...get any closer to the castle walls.

291
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:44,100
Yes, sir!

292
00:18:44,850 --> 00:18:47,390
My precious hawk is coming back to me...

293
00:18:47,390 --> 00:18:50,150
I'm not going to let him be killed for nothing.

294
00:18:55,610 --> 00:18:57,610
It's time, Captain!

295
00:18:58,030 --> 00:18:59,280
All companies, retreat!

296
00:18:59,280 --> 00:19:00,410
Regroup at the base camp!

297
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:03,580
Come on, men, get moving!

298
00:19:12,710 --> 00:19:14,790
The enemy is retreating!

299
00:19:14,790 --> 00:19:15,920
Start the pursuit!

300
00:19:16,210 --> 00:19:17,170
Strange!

301
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:19,670
They must have foreseen the consequences...

302
00:19:19,670 --> 00:19:22,010
...since they chose this particular strategy.

303
00:19:22,010 --> 00:19:26,350
Did the invincible White Hawk
really plot this scheme?

304
00:19:26,350 --> 00:19:28,020
I'm not going to contradict you...

305
00:19:28,020 --> 00:19:31,440
...but maybe you think
too highly of those men, General?

306
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:34,230
Nevertheless, just give us
the command to pursue them!

307
00:19:34,980 --> 00:19:37,320
If we let them get away...

308
00:19:37,320 --> 00:19:40,070
...the soldiers will be disgruntled
because they'll have missed out...

309
00:19:40,070 --> 00:19:41,610
...on their chance at glory!

310
00:19:42,070 --> 00:19:43,870
What are you doing, Boscone?

311
00:19:45,870 --> 00:19:47,240
Governor!

312
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:49,660
The enemy is retreating.

313
00:19:49,660 --> 00:19:51,920
Will you miss a chance
for victory just to observe them?

314
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:53,960
No, but...

315
00:19:55,250 --> 00:19:56,630
I order everyone!

316
00:19:57,250 --> 00:20:00,720
Do not kill the enemy's captain, Count Griffith!

317
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:03,050
Capture him alive!

318
00:20:05,390 --> 00:20:07,220
I promise that anyone who succeeds...

319
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:09,810
...in capturing him will be
immediately promoted two ranks!

320
00:20:09,810 --> 00:20:11,680
I will reward you with whatever you want!

321
00:20:12,730 --> 00:20:13,690
Governor!

322
00:20:14,060 --> 00:20:16,520
You should not promise such things.

323
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:17,480
I care not!

324
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:19,940
But it affects military discipline!

325
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:20,610
Boscone!

326
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:24,820
From now on, I am taking direct command!

327
00:20:25,450 --> 00:20:28,450
The Purple Rhino Knights are
to immediately pursue the enemy!

328
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:34,040
Notify the entire army of my orders!

329
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:35,080
Make sure it is enforced!

330
00:20:36,460 --> 00:20:37,460
General...

331
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:39,590
There's nothing we can do about this.

332
00:20:39,590 --> 00:20:42,050
All units, move to pursue the enemy!

333
00:20:46,590 --> 00:20:50,060
As rear guard, there are far too
many for me to take on alone...

334
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:55,600
But after everything, they are taking
the bait, just as Griffith planned.

335
00:20:57,770 --> 00:21:02,280
Yeah, everything was executed so
it would play perfectly into your hand...

336
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:03,440
As always...

337
00:21:06,030 --> 00:21:07,620
What a thrilling view!

338
00:21:08,990 --> 00:21:12,040
We're not going to deal with all of that, are we?

339
00:21:14,250 --> 00:21:15,620
Formations, regroup!

340
00:21:19,290 --> 00:21:20,960
We are reaching a crucial moment.

341
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:23,050
Our backs are to the river!

342
00:21:23,050 --> 00:21:24,300
There's no way to escape!

343
00:21:31,180 --> 00:21:32,390
Lay down your lives!

344
00:21:32,930 --> 00:21:35,310
If you don't, we are doomed!

345
00:21:35,850 --> 00:21:37,440
If we can survive...

346
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:38,810
...then we'll have won!

347
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

348
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

349
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

350
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

351
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

352
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

353
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

354
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

355
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

356
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

357
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

